---
description: Save buttons must show brief visual confirmation
alwaysApply: true
---

# Save button feedback

When the user presses a **Save** (or equivalent persist) control in the UI:

1. On success, give **visible confirmation** on the control itself (label and/or style change).
2. Revert to the normal label/style after a **short delay** (~1.5–2s).
3. Prefer a shared helper (e.g. `flashSaveButton(btn)`) over one-off copy.
4. Do not rely on silent success — no “did it save?” ambiguity.
5. On failure, keep the error path (alert / inline error); do not show the saved flash.

Example pattern:

```js
flashSaveButton(saveBtn); // → "Saved" + .is-just-saved, then restore
```
